    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear you. It's just that some people see it as a choice between helping someone halfway across the world or helping a struggling family in our own hometown. How would you frame the argument to show that one isn't more valid than the other, or that it's not just a zero-sum game where we're choosing foreign interests over our own?",
